Note that this means that your off-hand weapon would have to do less
than 4 damage on average (modulo the limited value of 5% bisection) for
the Tsurugi to be a better choice than twoweaponing.  Snick and a saber
or katana seems like a clear win here, especially with strength and
enchantment bonuses.

Personally I wouldn't bother switching saber/katana in the off-hand
based on the monster I'm facing, I'd just use the saber in Gehennom and
katana elsewhere.  Whichever I'm not using goes in the bag as a backup
in case of theft of Snick or the off-hand weapon.

Using 2 sabers in gehennom is also probably defensible (heck, my recent
rogue did fine with silver saber + silver dagger, for style).



